WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.767
-Our next guest is
a Grammy Award-winning musician

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.300
and songwriter and the front man
of the band Wilco.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.934
Their album "Cruel Country"
is out now.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.000
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.133
our friend Jeff Tweedy,
everybody.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:17.501
♪♪

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:22.801
♪♪

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.400
Welcome back, Jeff.
-Hey.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.968
-I want to start by asking,
do you remember this moment?

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.000
-No.
-No memory of it at all?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.033
-It doesn't --
Is that --

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.367
Who is that, Bill Hader?

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.367
It's not Bill Hader.
He was just here.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.067
It's Adam Scott.
-Oh.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.100
Cool.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.801
-Now, you worked
with Adam before.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.467
You also worked with Fred.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.634
-Oh.
-And -- Okay.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:50.834
But this is a true --

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:53.667
Fred used to open for Wilco
doing stand-up.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.133
-Yeah, I didn't know
he was gonna be here.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.434
-Oh, okay.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:01:00.234
Was it a weird vibe
back in the day?

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.968
-He owes my wife a lot of money.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.234
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.501
So this is a --
You --

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:10.634
This is true that Fred
made a promise to your wife.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:13.234
-He made a legal document.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.934
-Okay.
-Several times, we -- Yeah.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:19.400
-And, now, what was the impetus
of Fred making this --

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.400
-My wife gave him his start
in show business

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.200
by allowing him
to answer the phones

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.567
at the rock club that she owned.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.300
-Okay. This is true, Fred?
-True.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.467
-Okay, and so in return,
what did Fred promise your wife?

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.467
-Initially, he promised 50%
of all of his earnings.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:37.234
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.167
-And then when she
confronted him, about it...

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.934
-Sure, as you would
if he didn't pay up.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.634
-...he said he was sorry

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:48.100
and he would give her 75%.
-Got it.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.467
And, now, you've actually
brought the legal document?

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.601
-I do have the document with me.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.667
-Now, it is a video document.
-Yes.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.267
-And, Fred, you will confirm
that you made this?

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.968
-Yes.
-Okay. Here is Fred.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:01.534
And hopefully, if anybody here,
you know, passed the bar --

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.033
-I have my lawyer with me.
-Okay, great. Alright.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.701
Let's see if you believe
this is a legal document.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.901
-This is a legal document
without jokes,

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.968
without irony or sarcasm.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.601
This is not an exaggeration.

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.801
I, from now on,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.968
owe Susan Miller

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.033
75% of my income.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.133
It used to be 50%.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.200
It's up to 75%
because retroactively

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.300
going back to the amount
I owe her before,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.167
I need to add to that.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:32.434
That is all money brought in by
any comedy or any entertainment.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:33.534
That is what's owed.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.567
If you are a lawyer
looking at this,

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:38.567
there is no irony in my face
or, like, any winking.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.200
I owe this money.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.968
By the way, immediately.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.534
-I mean, I think
that's a legal document.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.734
-I -- Slam dunk.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.200
-But Fred's
a little shady, though.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.033
That's the problem.
Is it true that when Fred --

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.133
-How much could it be?

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.934
-How much could it be?
-10 grand?

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.501
-10 grand?
-Something in there, yeah.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:02:59.701
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.400
-You've made probably around
12 to 15 grand.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.133
-I would say 12 to 15.
-Yeah.

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.834
-So then you're getting
75% of that.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.434
You're gonna do pretty well.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:10.701
Fred -- Is it true that when
Fred used to open for you,

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.567
he would sometimes walk out
onstage and pretend to be you?

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.200
-Yes. Yes.
-Okay.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.634
So the audience is there
to see you.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.200
And what would Fred do?
-Fred would --

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.868
He would borrow my hat,
and I think he had a wig.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:27.367
And he would borrow my guitar

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:30.601
and he would go out onstage
and just go, "Hi."

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:35.968
"Jeff Tweedy.
I'm Jeff Tweedy."

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:38.067
And I think -- The sad part is,

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.267
I think a lot of people
really thought it was me

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:44.000
because -- I don't know.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.133
I guess he's
a pretty good mimic.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.033
-Yeah, he's a pretty good mimic.
-Yeah.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:51.701
-I also want to see if I can get
confirmation on this from you,

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:54.133
that despite winning Grammys,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.367
you had something that I
only thought existed in legend.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:02.868
You had a Chipotle burrito --
free burrito card.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.167
-I did.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.501
-And so explain how it worked
and how you got it.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:09.000
-I don't know how I got it.
-Okay.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.133
-It showed up in the mail
one day in a carved wooden box,

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.467
like something you would see,

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:17.167
like, an immunity challenge
amulet or something.

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.567
And you opened it up,

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:23.100
and it said, "Jeff Tweedy's free
burrito card from Chipotle,"

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.467
and you would take it.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.167
-Were you nervous the
first time you presented it?

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.701
-Yeah, I was a little nervous.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.400
And it never --

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.968
it never got easy using it
because every single person

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.067
that you would hand it to
at the register would go,

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:37.067
"What the [bleep] is this?"

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:43.033
And you'd go, "Just scan it.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.467
Trust me, just scan it."

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.067
And they would scan it, and
they'd go, "What the [bleep]"

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.133
'Cause it would come up
100% discount.

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:52.467
-Wow.
-Celebrity discount.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:53.667
-It would say
celebrity discount?

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.267
-100% celebrity discount.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.601
So I'd buy burritos
for everybody in line

00:04:57.601 --> 00:05:01.968
and for my children's school
and stuff like that, yeah.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:04.667
-Did they know who you were?

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:05.934
-The people at the counter?
-Yeah.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:06.934
-Oh, no.
-Okay.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.501
-No, never. Never.

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.701
And so that would be --
The other half of the story

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:14.100
would be that a lot of times
we'd be sitting there eating

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.200
and they would be
back in the kitchen

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.767
trying to figure out who I am.

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.334
-Right.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:25.534
-And unfortunately, one of
the main things that comes up,

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:29.467
I think, when you Google my
name, at least for a long time,

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:33.300
it has been me singing
Black Eyed Peas songs.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.534
-Yeah, you did, like, a charity
event where you played.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:39.234
-I did a charity event
for my friend Dan Sinker,

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:41.167
who made a book
about Rahm Emanuel

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.667
and the mayor race in Chicago.

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:46.834
And one of the bits
in his tweets

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:49.234
that he had done throughout
the campaign was that,

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:53.734
"That ass[bleep] Tweedy won't
do any Black Eyed Peas songs."

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:55.667
So he put together --
when he put out a book

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.367
of all of those tweets,

00:05:57.367 --> 00:05:59.601
he asked me
if I would play a show

00:05:59.601 --> 00:06:01.400
and do Black Eyed Peas songs.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.067
So I said sure.
And I tried to do it.

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:07.000
It was out of --
It was not my skill set.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.400
-Yeah. Do you mind
if we show a clip?

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.701
Because I was
very excited to hear

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.167
that you covered
Black Eyed Peas.

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.534
-Sure.
-You did -- I will say,

00:06:12.534 --> 00:06:13.968
I thought it was
a beautiful match.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.133
Let's take a look.

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:17.267
-Tonight's the night.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:19.467
Let's live it up.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:21.300
I got my money.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.767
Let's spend it up.

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:28.033
Go out and smash it
like, "Oh, my God."

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:31.367
Jump off that sofa.
Let's kick it off.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:32.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:33.901
-Beautiful.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:36.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:38.601
-Yeah, so --

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:40.300
so they -- so they --

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.667
so everybody in the kitchen
would come out and want to --

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:45.667
"You're the
'I Gotta Feeling' guy."

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.067
-So wait.
So the Chipotle staff

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:48.834
then thought you were
in Black Eyed Peas.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.701
-They thought I wrote that song.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.567
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:54.300
-That's what would happen.
I mean, it happened --

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.734
It happened once.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.067
-Thank you for your honesty.
Thank you for your honesty.

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:02.601
-But yeah, because it happened
once, I can say it happened.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:03.968
-Yeah, you can say it happened.

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:05.501
Yeah, legally you can
say it happened.

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:08.501
-But from that point on,
we just got stuff to go.

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:09.934
-Yeah, that's smart.
Yeah.

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:11.734
You don't want to put yourself
in that awkward situation.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.634
-Just got out of the way
while they figured it out.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.634
-Do you -- Are you ever
in a restaurant

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:19.801
where you hear your music?

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:21.667
-Occasionally, but I'm not --

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:24.234
I'm always the last one
to pick it out.

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:25.667
-Ah.

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:28.567
-I'll be like, "What is this?"

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.033
And my kids -- "It's you."

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:34.567
-That must be
a weird moment for your kids.

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.434
They're like,
"What's wrong with you?"

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:38.634
-I think -- Yeah,
I think they're used to that.

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:43.801
The card stopped working, too,
by the way.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.334
That was an awkward --
That was an awkward day.

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.601
-Oh, my God.

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:50.801
Yeah. "Just scan it again.
Trust me."

00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:52.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:55.067
You're like,
"I'm a big-time celebrity."

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:57.734
-No, trust --
Just scan it again.

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.267
-Did you try multiple days,

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.767
or did the one day it stopped
working, did you let it go then?

00:08:01.767 --> 00:08:04.434
-I went to a different Chipotle.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:06.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.701
Tried it again.

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:10.868
-That is a day
I hope you were on your own.

00:08:10.868 --> 00:08:12.234
You didn't have your kids
with you.

00:08:12.234 --> 00:08:13.868
Like, "Don't worry, boys.
It'll work at the next one."

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:17.434
-I was on the hook for a whole
restaurant full of burritos.

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:18.734
-Oh, no.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.267
You promised it to the store
before you checked it.

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.033
You're like,
"Burritos for everyone!"

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:23.868
-Exactly.

00:08:23.868 --> 00:08:27.501
The only times I've ever been
a big shot in a restaurant.

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:30.133
-Well, I'm very happy you guys
are gonna be out here

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:31.400
playing another song for us.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.901
It's always such a joy
to have you here.

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:34.968
Thank you for making the time.
You guys, Jeff Tweedy.

